      "append_only": false,
      "notes": "Written for whoever is woken at 3am, which is why symptoms come first: the reader knows what they are seeing, not what it is called. `last_exercised` exists because a runbook nobody has followed is a document rather than a procedure, and the steps that have quietly stopped working are invisible until someone tries them. Remediation steps that need approval say so inline, so the reader does not discover the gate halfway through an outage. It carries no approval: reliability-reviewer records a verdict, and a verdict is not an approval. A runbook needing sign-off before anyone may follow it would be a runbook nobody reads during an outage."
    }
